<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  A Tauri app under the hardened runtime is a Rust binary plus a system webview,
  and the web content runs in Apple's own out-of-process service — so it needs
  none of the JIT / unsigned-memory / library-validation exceptions that an
  Electron app or a process linking its own ML runtime does. Verified
  empirically on Publik's Iris: the hardened-runtime build launches and runs
  fine with an empty plist.

  Do not add entitlements speculatively. Every one you add is something Apple
  scrutinises at notarization and something the verify script has to assert
  survived the build.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
